          "width": "hug"
        },
        "children": [
          "{children}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "ComposerPicker",
      "note": "Subtle inline dropdown. Ships as a WinUI subtle DropDownButton (a transparent Button that opens a flyout), NOT a bordered ComboBox and NOT a Fluent-web pill/segmented control. Shows the current value in `muted` secondary text (TextFillColorSecondary) with a trailing `muted` chevron (Segoe Fluent \\uE70D, previewed ~10px). 32px min height; horizontal padding token `2`, gap token `1`; `sm` radius = WinUI ControlCornerRadius (4px). It is a real `button` whose browser chrome is removed with `control.chrome:none`, so the transparent WinUI rest state (SubtleFillColorTransparent, `$none`) shows with no web button border, and `control.focus` supplies the Windows accent focus rectangle instead of a web focus ring. Hover uses `subtleHover` (SubtleFillColorSecondary) and press uses `subtlePressed` (SubtleFillColorTertiary) through `states`, so the picker stays quiet in the composer toolbar and never competes with the primary Send action. When there is nothing to choose (for example the session picker with a single session) the picker is disabled and its value reads a shade lighter than the enabled muted text. Used for the model, reasoning-effort, and session selectors; `on.click` opens an in-app single-select (RadioMenuItem) flyout. ComposerPickerOptions is a representative shared option list because flyout targets take no props; the real per-picker option sets (sessions, models, effort levels) are supplied by the app and are a Reactor port note.",
      "props": {
        "label": "Model"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "composer-picker-root",
        "el": "button",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "button",
          "aria-haspopup": "listbox",
          "aria-label": "{label}"
        },
        "layout": {
          "mode": "horizontal",
          "gap": "1",
          "padding": {
            "left": "2",
            "right": "2"
          },
          "align": "center",
          "height": 32,
          "width": "hug"
        },
        "appearance": {
          "fontFamily": "body",
          "textStyle": "small",
          "color": "muted",
          "background": "$none",
          "radius": "sm"
        },
        "control": {
          "chrome": "none",
          "focus": {
            "kind": "outline",
            "color": "accent"
          }
        },
        "states": {
          "hover": {
            "background": "subtleHover"
          },
          "pressed": {
            "background": "subtlePressed"
          },
          "hoverPressed": {
            "background": "subtlePressed"
          },
          "disabled": {
            "color": "muted",
            "background": "$none"
          }
        },
        "on": {
          "click": {
            "open": "ComposerPickerOptions"
          }
        },
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "composer-picker-label",
            "el": "span",
            "children": [
              "{label}"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "composer-picker-chevron",
            "el": "svg",
            "attrs": {
              "width": "12",
              "height": "12",
              "viewBox": "0 0 24 24",
              "fill": "none",
              "aria-hidden": "true",
              "stroke": "currentColor",
              "stroke-width": "2",
              "stroke-linecap": "round",
              "stroke-linejoin": "round"
            },
            "appearance": {
              "color": "muted"
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "composer-picker-chevron-path",
                "el": "path",
                "attrs": {
                  "d": "M6 9l6 6 6-6"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "ComposerPickerOptions",
      "note": "Representative single-select flyout for the subtle composer pickers (model, session, reasoning-effort). Ships as a WinUI Flyout of RadioMenuItem rows on a `surface` (CardBackgroundFillColorDefault) sheet with `md` overlay radius and `md` shadow. Each row reserves a leading glyph column; the selected row shows an `accent` Segoe Fluent Icons CheckMark (glyph U+E73E, WinUI SymbolThemeFontFamily selection glyph, not a radio dot) while unselected rows keep the column empty so labels stay aligned. The check glyph carries a font-family-only raw style because the icon font is outside the display/body/mono token set (documented as the `icon` typography family in design.json); color stays token-bound to `accent`. Selecting a row closes the flyout; reopening restores defaults. Because `on.click.open` targets take no props, this shows a representative model list; the real per-picker option sets (sessions, models, effort levels) are supplied by the app and are a Reactor port note.",
      "root": {
        "id": "composer-picker-options",
